<title>BELGIUM: BELGIAN FEB CAR REGISTRATIONS DOWN 11.9% YR/YR.</title>
<headline>BELGIAN FEB CAR REGISTRATIONS DOWN 11.9% YR/YR.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-03-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Belgian new car registrations</p>
<p>fell 11.9 percent in February compared to the same month in</p>
<p>1996, according to figures released on Tuesday from the Belgian</p>
<p>Federation of Automobile Manufacturers (Febiac).</p>
<p>    BELGIAN NEW CAR REGISTRATIONS	FEB 1997     FEB 1996</p>
<p>    month					39,124	 44,396</p>
<p>The following manufacturers had a market share of over three</p>
<p>percent in the month</p>
<p> VW	7,855 (20.1 pct)  vs   8,029  (18.1 pct)</p>
<p> Peugeot 6,095 (15.6 pct)  vs   8,438  (19.0 pct)</p>
<p> GM	4,346 (11.1 pct)  vs   4,044   (9.1 pct)</p>
<p> Renault 4,018 (10.3 pct)  vs   4,475  (10.1 pct)</p>
<p> Ford Motor 3,492  (8.9 pct)  vs   4,020   (9.1 pct)</p>
<p> Fiat    2,014  (5.1 pct)  vs   1,774   (4.0 pct)</p>
<p> Toyota  1,953  (5.0 pct)  vs   2,550   (5.7 pct)</p>
<p> BMW     1,755  (4.5 pct)  vs   2,053   (4.6 pct)</p>
<p> Nissan  1,568  (4.0 pct)  vs   1,690   (3.8 pct)</p>
<p>-- Brussels Newsroom +32 2 287 6810, Fax +32 2 230 7710</p>
</text>
